    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273-a1">

                <pb facs="0499" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg437"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    40.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carrié to Mr.
                            Langston</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of the Secretary of State of the Department of Finance and
                                Commerce and Foreign Affairs, Republic of Hayti</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-03-14"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 14, 1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">Liberty, Equality, Fraternity.</p>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister of the United States</hi>: As no doubt
                    you have already learned by public report, General Louis Tanis, sr., military
                    commandant of this department, revolted last night against the authority of the
                    government. Beaten on every hand, this general has taken refuge in the Fort
                    National, where, it would seem, it will be <pb facs="0500" n="438"
                        xml:id="pg438"/> necessary, to dislodge him, to use force, and cause the
                    painful alternative of bloodshed. Before coming to this extremity my department
                    has resolved to inform you of the situation, requesting you to communicate the
                    same to your diplomatic colleagues, in order that you may come to some
                    understanding with them and take measures governed by circumstances having in
                    view the interests of humanity.</p>
                <p>This dispatch is strictly confidential.</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item>F. CARRIÉ.</item>
                            <item>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">John M. Langston</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Minister Resident, &amp;c., &amp;c., of the
                                    United States, Port au Prince.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
